{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cd /workspace && cat packet/incident_packet.md && echo \"---\" && cat packet/findings.json'","aggregated_output":"# Incident Packet: INC-2047\n\n## Triggering Condition\nBulk-refund requests were accepted without idempotency keys due to the `legacy_batch_header` bypass, resulting in duplicate refunds for three enterprise accounts.\n\n## Failed Guardrail\nThe idempotency-required guardrail was skipped at 10:18 UTC when the `legacy_batch_header` was present, allowing duplicate refund requests to be processed.\n\n## Highest-Confidence Follow-up Action\nReject all bulk-refund requests that do not include an idempotency key, and remove the `legacy_batch_header` bypass before re-enabling the bulk-refund endpoint.\n\n## Unresolved Ambiguity\nThe initial theory of queue worker replay (TICKET-8721) was opened before API gateway logs were available and has been superseded by evidence from TICKET-8729 showing the duplicate refunds were caused by missing idempotency keys rather than worker replay.\n---\n{\n  \"ranked_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"finding\": \"Bulk-refund requests accepted without idempotency keys due to legacy_batch_header bypass\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"evidence\": [\"corpus/timeline/incident_timeline.md\", \"corpus/tickets/TICKET-8729.md\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding\": \"Idempotency-required guardrail was skipped at 10:18 UTC\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"evidence\": [\"corpus/timeline/incident_timeline.md\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding\": \"Duplicate refunds affected three enterprise accounts\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"evidence\": [\"corpus/tickets/TICKET-8721.md\", \"corpus/tickets/TICKET-8729.md\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unresolved_ambiguity\": \"Initial queue worker replay theory (TICKET-8721) was opened before API gateway logs were available; evidence from TICKET-8729 supersedes this theory\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
